  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Expressed in **ascending order** in radians, the **exact solutions** to the equation  $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(2x)=-1,$ for $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi ,$  are\n\n${x}_{1}=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,{x}_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}$,\\,{x}_{3}=$\n{{field-3}}$,\\,{x}_{4}=$\n{{field-4}}.",
  "worked_solution": "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{8}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(4n-1)\\pi }{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,\u2026,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=-1$ gives $x=-\\frac{5\\pi }{8}$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{8}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{8}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{8}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi .$ \n\nSo, in ascending order,  the solutions are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-\\frac{5\\pi }{8},\\,{x}_{2}=-\\frac{\\pi }{8},\\,{x}_{3}=\\frac{3\\pi }{8},\\,{x}_{4}=\\frac{7\\pi }{8}\n$$",
